{% extends "tutorial_base.html.j2" %}

{% block tutorial_body %}
        <!-- Intro Card -->
        <div class="doc-intro-card">
          <h2>Write Your Own Controller Post in Sandboxed Lua 5.4</h2>
          <p>
            Need a custom M-code for an older plasma table, a shop-built floating head, or a specific IHS probe cycle? Write a single <code class="mono">.lua</code> post-processor and run it on both <strong>2D Flat Sheet</strong> and <strong>4-Axis Rotary Tube/Structural</strong> jobs with Pack Mode parity built in.
          </p>
          <p style="margin-top: 0.75rem;">
            Your custom post runs on the exact same <code class="mono">api_version = 1</code> Lua 5.4 contract that powers RotaryCAM&rsquo;s built-in controllers. If you have ever edited a SheetCam <code class="mono">.scpost</code> file, the hook layout will feel familiar right away.
          </p>

          <ul class="doc-bullet-list" style="margin-top: 0.85rem;">
            <li><strong>Built for both 2D plate and 4-axis rotary:</strong> One post handles flat sheet, round pipe, HSS, open beams, and multi-stick Pack Mode without maintaining separate files.</li>
            <li><strong>Strictly sandboxed:</strong> No filesystem (<code class="mono">io</code>), no OS shell (<code class="mono">os</code>), and no external modules (<code class="mono">package</code>). Each run is capped at <code class="mono">4 MB</code> of memory and <code class="mono">2,000,000</code> VM instructions, so accidental infinite loops abort cleanly in milliseconds.</li>
            <li><strong>Included in every paid tier:</strong> Custom Lua post-processors are unlocked on both <strong>Maker ($199)</strong> and <strong>Pro Shop ($399)</strong> licenses.</li>
          </ul>

          <div class="doc-intro-grid">
            <div class="doc-intro-stat">
              <span class="label">Runtime Contract</span>
              <span class="value">Sandboxed Lua 5.4 (<code class="mono">api_version = 1</code>)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-intro-stat">
              <span class="label">Sandbox Guardrails</span>
              <span class="value">4 MB RAM &bull; 2,000,000 VM Ops &bull; Zero I/O</span>
            </div>
            <div class="doc-intro-stat">
              <span class="label">License Access</span>
              <span class="value">Maker &amp; Pro Shop</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 1: ANATOMY OF A .LUA POST-PROCESSOR
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-1">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 01</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Anatomy of a <code class="mono">.lua</code> Post-Processor (<code class="mono">api_version = 1</code>)</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Every custom post starts with a global <code class="mono">post</code> table. Only <code class="mono">api_version</code>, <code class="mono">id</code>, and <code class="mono">name</code> are required; all 34 remaining options fall back to safe RS-274 defaults when omitted.
            </p>

            <div class="doc-code-block">
              <div class="doc-code-bar">
                <span class="doc-code-title"><span class="dot"></span> Starter Metadata Table (Required + Common Fields)</span>
                <span class="doc-code-lang">Lua 5.4</span>
              </div>
              <pre><code>post = {
  api_version      = 1,
  id               = "shop_custom_thc",
  name             = "Shop Custom Plasma + THC",
  description      = "G38.2 touch-off with ref-distance skip and M62/M63 THC sync",
  file_extension   = "nc",
  base_dialect     = "generic_g94",
  comment_style    = "parens",             -- "parens", "semicolon", "brackets", "semicolon_and_parens"
  rotary_feed_mode = "inverse_time_g93",   -- "modal_g94" or "inverse_time_g93"
  z_model          = "explicit",           -- "explicit" or "controller"
}</code></pre>
            </div>

            <p style="margin-top: 1rem;">
              Below is the complete reference for all <strong>37 options</strong> accepted in <code class="mono">post = { ... }</code>.
            </p>

            <h3 style="color: #fff; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.45rem;">A. Identity &amp; Base Dialect (6 Fields)</h3>
            <div class="table-wrap" style="margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;">
              <table class="doc-table">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th style="min-width: 175px;">Field</th>
                    <th style="min-width: 195px;">Type &amp; Allowed Values</th>
                    <th style="min-width: 105px;">Default</th>
                    <th>What It Controls on Your Table</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">api_version</code></td>
                    <td>Integer (<code class="mono">1</code>)</td>
                    <td><strong>Required</strong></td>
                    <td>Contract version checked when loading your script. Must be <code class="mono">1</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">id</code></td>
                    <td>Slug <code class="mono">[a-z0-9_-]{1,48}</code> (cannot be <code class="mono">"validate"</code>)</td>
                    <td><strong>Required</strong></td>
                    <td>Unique ID saved in machine profiles (<code class="mono">post_processor_id</code>) and REST API URLs.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">name</code></td>
                    <td>Non-empty String</td>
                    <td><strong>Required</strong></td>
                    <td>Label shown in the <strong>Controller / Post-Processor</strong> dropdown.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">description</code></td>
                    <td>String</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">""</code></td>
                    <td>Short controller and table summary shown in the Post Processors list.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">file_extension</code></td>
                    <td>1..8 ASCII alphanumeric chars (<code class="mono">"nc"</code>, <code class="mono">"tap"</code>, <code class="mono">"ngc"</code>)</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"nc"</code></td>
                    <td>Output file extension for single-part and Pack Mode downloads (lowercased automatically).</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">base_dialect</code></td>
                    <td>
                      One of 14 built-in IDs:<br>
                      <code class="mono">"simcnc"</code>, <code class="mono">"linuxcnc_qtplasmac"</code>, <code class="mono">"langmuir_firecontrol"</code>, <code class="mono">"mach4_ess"</code>, <code class="mono">"masso_g3"</code>, <code class="mono">"mach3"</code>, <code class="mono">"centroid_acorn"</code>, <code class="mono">"grblhal"</code>, <code class="mono">"uccnc"</code>, <code class="mono">"flashcut"</code>, <code class="mono">"edingcnc"</code>, <code class="mono">"planetcnc"</code>, <code class="mono">"shopsabre_wincnc"</code>, <code class="mono">"generic_g94"</code>
                    </td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"generic_g94"</code></td>
                    <td>Inherits controller touch-off strategy, THC lock syntax, scribe on/off codes, work-origin policy, and flat corner blending for any hooks you omit.</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>

            <h3 style="color: #fff; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.45rem;">B. Comments, Framing &amp; Line Sanitization (8 Fields)</h3>
            <div class="table-wrap" style="margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;">
              <table class="doc-table">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th style="min-width: 195px;">Field</th>
                    <th style="min-width: 175px;">Type &amp; Allowed Values</th>
                    <th style="min-width: 95px;">Default</th>
                    <th>What It Controls on Your Table</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">comment_style</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"parens"</code>, <code class="mono">"semicolon"</code>, <code class="mono">"brackets"</code>, <code class="mono">"semicolon_and_parens"</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"parens"</code></td>
                    <td>Enforces comment delimiters (<code class="mono">(text)</code>, <code class="mono">; text</code>, <code class="mono">[text]</code>, or both <code class="mono">;</code> and <code class="mono">()</code>) in output sanitization and <code class="mono">GCodeGrammarLinter</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">percent_framing</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"none"</code>, <code class="mono">"both"</code>, <code class="mono">"trailing"</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"none"</code></td>
                    <td>Adds <code class="mono">%</code> at top and bottom (<code class="mono">"both"</code>), at EOF only (<code class="mono">"trailing"</code>), or omits <code class="mono">%</code> completely (<code class="mono">"none"</code>).</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">trailing_newline</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>Appends a final newline (<code class="mono">\n</code>) after the last G-code line or trailing <code class="mono">%</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">max_line_length</code></td>
                    <td>Integer <code class="mono">&gt;= 0</code> or <code class="mono">nil</code> (<code class="mono">0</code> = unlimited)</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">nil</code></td>
                    <td>Caps line length (for example <code class="mono">80</code> chars on GRBL or legacy RS-274). Lines over the cap are trimmed unless <code class="mono">preserve_coord_lines_over_max</code> applies.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">strip_realtime_chars</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>Strips realtime command bytes (<code class="mono">!</code>, <code class="mono">~</code>, <code class="mono">?</code>, Ctrl-X) from comments so controllers like grblHAL do not pause or reset mid-cut.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">uppercase_ascii_comments</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>Converts emitted comment text to strict uppercase ASCII for older controls.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">preserve_coord_lines_over_max</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>Keeps <code class="mono">G0/G1/G2/G3</code> coordinate lines intact if they exceed <code class="mono">max_line_length</code> instead of truncating axis words.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">converts_parens_to_semicolon</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>Rewrites <code class="mono">(...)</code> comments into <code class="mono">; ...</code> during final sanitization (useful on semicolon-only controls like Centroid Acorn).</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>

            <h3 style="color: #fff; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.45rem;">C. Rotary, Feedrate &amp; Motion Guardrails (9 Fields)</h3>
            <div class="table-wrap" style="margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;">
              <table class="doc-table">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th style="min-width: 195px;">Field</th>
                    <th style="min-width: 175px;">Type &amp; Allowed Values</th>
                    <th style="min-width: 95px;">Default</th>
                    <th>What It Controls on Your Table</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">rotary_feed_mode</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"modal_g94"</code>, <code class="mono">"inverse_time_g93"</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"modal_g94"</code></td>
                    <td>Selects standard units/min (<code class="mono">G94</code>) or inverse-time (<code class="mono">G93</code>) feedrate on 4-axis rotary cuts. Overridden by <code class="mono">forces_modal_g94_only</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">g93_scope</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"program"</code>, <code class="mono">"stroke_only"</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"program"</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"program"</code> stays in <code class="mono">G93</code> across rotary strokes; <code class="mono">"stroke_only"</code> drops back to <code class="mono">G94</code> between cuts for safe probing and rapids.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">rotary_axis_letter</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"A"</code>, <code class="mono">"B"</code>, <code class="mono">"W"</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"A"</code></td>
                    <td>Axis letter used on rotary moves and <code class="mono">G92</code> zeroing (for example <code class="mono">"W"</code> on WinCNC SideKick).</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">force_rotary_y_wrap</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>Forces concentric round tube cuts onto linear <code class="mono">Y</code> wrap (<code class="mono">Y = R * A_rad</code>) instead of 4th-axis degrees.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">forces_modal_g94_only</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>Locks the post to <code class="mono">G94</code> everywhere (ignores <code class="mono">inverse_time_g93</code> and enables 2.5&deg; angular subdivision).</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">strict_rs274_cartesian_feed</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>Enforces strict RS-274 Cartesian feed rules, rotary angular snapping, and 2.5&deg; angular subdivision.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">ensure_safe_z_before_rotary_rapid</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>Inserts a safe-Z retract before any rapid move that rotates the A/B/W chuck.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">micro_move_min_mm</code></td>
                    <td>Number <code class="mono">&gt;= 0.0</code> (mm)</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">0.0</code></td>
                    <td>Filters out sub-threshold micro motion segments below this length and enables modal word compression when <code class="mono">&gt; 0</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">g93_linear_deadband_mm</code></td>
                    <td>Number <code class="mono">&gt;= 0.0</code> (mm)</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">0.0</code></td>
                    <td>Minimum linear chord deadband (mm) before <code class="mono">G93</code> inverse-time feed calculation applies.</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>

            <h3 style="color: #fff; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.45rem;">D. Z-Axis, Touch-Off Probing &amp; Dwell (8 Fields)</h3>
            <div class="table-wrap" style="margin: 0.5rem 0 1rem;">
              <table class="doc-table">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th style="min-width: 195px;">Field</th>
                    <th style="min-width: 175px;">Type &amp; Allowed Values</th>
                    <th style="min-width: 95px;">Default</th>
                    <th>What It Controls on Your Table</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">z_model</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"explicit"</code>, <code class="mono">"controller"</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"explicit"</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"explicit"</code> emits full CAM surface + standoff Z heights; <code class="mono">"controller"</code> lets controller macros own flat Z and emits delta Z on 4D/ramped cuts.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">dwell_unit</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"seconds"</code>, <code class="mono">"milliseconds"</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"seconds"</code></td>
                    <td>Controls whether built-in pierce dwells emit decimal seconds (<code class="mono">G4 P0.500</code>) or integer milliseconds (<code class="mono">G4 P500</code>).</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">dwell_g_word</code></td>
                    <td>String</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"G4"</code></td>
                    <td>G-code word emitted for built-in dwell lines (such as <code class="mono">"G4"</code> or <code class="mono">"G04"</code>).</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">dwell_param_word</code></td>
                    <td>String</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"P"</code></td>
                    <td>Parameter letter emitted on built-in dwell lines (such as <code class="mono">"P"</code> or <code class="mono">"X"</code>).</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">default_probe_gcode</code></td>
                    <td>String</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"G38.2"</code></td>
                    <td>Fallback probe word used by <code class="mono">ctx.emit_explicit_probe</code> when touch-off strategy is not <code class="mono">probe_g38_2</code>, <code class="mono">probe_g31</code>, or <code class="mono">home_g28_1</code> (e.g., <code class="mono">"G31.0"</code>).</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">probes_relative_to_pierce_surface</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>When <code class="mono">true</code>, <code class="mono">ctx.emit_explicit_probe</code> searches down to <code class="mono">pierce_surface_z - search_dist</code> (with pre-probe retract for <code class="mono">G31</code>); when <code class="mono">false</code>, searches to <code class="mono">-search_dist</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">uses_direct_g92_switch_offset</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>When <code class="mono">true</code>, compensates float switch travel in one line (<code class="mono">G92 Z(pierce_surface_z - switch_offset)</code>) instead of <code class="mono">G92 Z0</code> + rapid lift + <code class="mono">G92</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">restores_g94_before_safe_z</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>Restores <code class="mono">G94</code> feed mode before retracting to <code class="mono">safe_z</code> at the end of a cut.</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>

            <h3 style="color: #fff; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.45rem;">E. Kerf, Scribe &amp; Program Structure (6 Fields)</h3>
            <div class="table-wrap" style="margin: 0.5rem 0 0;">
              <table class="doc-table">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th style="min-width: 215px;">Field</th>
                    <th style="min-width: 175px;">Type &amp; Allowed Values</th>
                    <th style="min-width: 95px;">Default</th>
                    <th>What It Controls on Your Table</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">supports_hardware_kerf</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>Enables controller-side <code class="mono">G41</code>/<code class="mono">G42</code> cutter compensation via <code class="mono">on_hardware_kerf</code> or built-in <code class="mono">D</code>/<code class="mono">P</code> words.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">supports_scribe_g52</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">true</code></td>
                    <td>Uses <code class="mono">G52</code> temporary work offsets for pneumatic scribe XY nozzle offsets when <code class="mono">true</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">bakes_scribe_xy_offset</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>When <code class="mono">supports_scribe_g52 = false</code> and this is <code class="mono">true</code>, bakes the scribe XY nozzle offset directly into emitted coordinates.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">emits_program_end_safe_z_before_footer</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">true</code></td>
                    <td>Emits <code class="mono">G0 Z&lt;safe_z&gt;</code> right before <code class="mono">on_footer(ctx)</code> runs. Set <code class="mono">false</code> if your footer handles safe retract itself.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">preamble_sentinel_line</code></td>
                    <td>String or <code class="mono">nil</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">nil</code></td>
                    <td>Optional literal Line 1 header inserted above <code class="mono">ROTARYCAM SIM</code> (for example <code class="mono">"(v1.6-sc)"</code> for FireControl).</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">program_end_codes</code></td>
                    <td>Array of Strings (non-empty)</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">{"M30", "M2", "M02"}</code></td>
                    <td>EOF program-end codes accepted by <code class="mono">GCodeGrammarLinter</code> (for example add <code class="mono">"M60"</code> on EdingCNC or <code class="mono">"M66"</code> on WinCNC).</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 2: LIFECYCLE HOOKS, ON_CAPABILITIES & CTX / RC API
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-2">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 02</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Lifecycle Hooks, <code class="mono">on_capabilities</code>, <code class="mono">ctx</code> &amp; <code class="mono">rc</code> Helpers</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Every hook function is optional. Omit any hook you do not need, and RotaryCAM falls back to clean RS-274 defaults so you only write the lines that differ on your controller.
            </p>

            <div class="doc-callout tip" style="margin: 0.85rem 0 1.1rem;">
              <div class="doc-callout-title">Two-Stage Compilation Order (Important for State)</div>
              <p>
                RotaryCAM compiles body cuts first (<strong>Stage 1:</strong> <code class="mono">on_piece_start</code>, <code class="mono">on_pierce</code>, <code class="mono">on_torch_off</code>, <code class="mono">on_between_pieces</code>) so it can measure exact rotary bounds, and then runs <strong>Stage 2</strong> (<code class="mono">on_preamble</code>, <code class="mono">on_preamble_post_sim</code>, <code class="mono">on_footer</code>). Initialize Lua counters at script top level (<code class="mono">local pierce_count = 0</code>) or inside <code class="mono">on_piece_start</code> rather than resetting them inside <code class="mono">on_preamble</code>.
              </p>
            </div>

            <h3 style="color: #fff; font-size: 1.1rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">1. Lifecycle Hooks</h3>
            <div class="table-wrap" style="margin: 0.75rem 0;">
              <table class="doc-table">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th style="min-width: 245px;">Hook Signature</th>
                    <th>When It Runs &amp; Return Contract</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">on_capabilities(ctx)</code></td>
                    <td>Computes dynamic per-job or per-feature capabilities from <code class="mono">ctx.settings</code> and <code class="mono">ctx.stock</code>. Returns an optional capability override table (see Section 2 below).</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">on_validate(ctx)</code></td>
                    <td>Runs before generation. Return a non-empty error string to block unsupported stock profiles or machine settings, or <code class="mono">nil</code> to proceed.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">on_preamble(ctx)</code><br><code class="mono">on_preamble_post_sim(ctx)</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">on_preamble</code> emits modal setup (<code class="mono">G20/G21</code>, <code class="mono">G90</code>, <code class="mono">G40</code>, <code class="mono">G94</code>, <code class="mono">ctx.rotary_zero_line</code>, safe Z). <code class="mono">on_preamble_post_sim</code> emits extra lines right after <code class="mono">ROTARYCAM SIM</code>. Returns <code class="mono">nil</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">on_piece_start(ctx)</code><br><code class="mono">on_between_pieces(ctx)</code><br><code class="mono">on_post_piece_wrap(ctx)</code></td>
                    <td>Pack Mode and stick transition hooks. Emit per-piece headers (<code class="mono">ctx.piece_index</code> / <code class="mono">ctx.total_pieces</code>), reset rotary/probe state between packed parts, or unwrap rotary after the last piece. Returns <code class="mono">nil</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">on_intra_body_rotary_reset(ctx)</code></td>
                    <td>Optional custom modulo-360&deg; rotary coordinate reset between features on the same stick (receives <code class="mono">ctx.rotary_axis_letter</code> and <code class="mono">ctx.mod_deg_formatted</code>). Returns <code class="mono">nil</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">on_pre_cut_setup(ctx)</code></td>
                    <td>Runs before positioning to the pierce point. Receives <code class="mono">ctx.feature_name</code>, <code class="mono">ctx.feature_cut_feed</code>, <code class="mono">ctx.feat_dynamic_z</code>, <code class="mono">ctx.is_entry_ramped</code>, <code class="mono">ctx.is_small_hole</code>, <code class="mono">ctx.is_plasma_mark</code>. Returns <code class="mono">nil</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">on_pierce(ctx)</code></td>
                    <td>Performs IHS touch-off, pierce height move, <code class="mono">ctx.emit_edge_start_move()</code> if <code class="mono">ctx.has_edge_start_move</code>, <code class="mono">M3</code> ignition, dwell (<code class="mono">ctx.effective_dwell_sec</code>), plunge if <code class="mono">ctx.should_emit_vertical_plunge</code>, and optional <code class="mono">G93</code> entry. Return <code class="mono">{ initial_thc_locked = true/false }</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">on_torch_off(ctx)</code></td>
                    <td>Locks THC if <code class="mono">not ctx.thc_locked</code>, turns torch off (<code class="mono">M5</code>), and restores <code class="mono">G94</code> if needed. Return <code class="mono">{ thc_locked = true/false }</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">on_thc_lock(ctx)</code><br><code class="mono">on_thc_unlock(ctx)</code><br><code class="mono">on_inline_thc_suffix(ctx)</code></td>
                    <td>Standalone THC lock/unlock hooks (<code class="mono">ctx.reason</code> tags corners, small holes, or voids), or <code class="mono">on_inline_thc_suffix</code> returning an inline suffix string (e.g., for Mach3/WinCNC) or <code class="mono">nil</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">on_post_arc_ok_check(ctx)</code><br><code class="mono">on_should_check_post_ramp_thc_unlock(ctx)</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">on_post_arc_ok_check</code> emits THC lock lines after the initial Arc-OK step. <code class="mono">on_should_check_post_ramp_thc_unlock</code> returns <code class="mono">true</code>/<code class="mono">false</code> using <code class="mono">ctx.is_entry_ramped</code> and <code class="mono">ctx.seg_idx</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">on_void_arc_ok_ignore(ctx)</code><br><code class="mono">on_void_arc_ok_restore(ctx)</code></td>
                    <td>Disables and re-enables Arc-OK transfer failure detection when crossing a previously cut kerf void. Returns <code class="mono">nil</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">on_hardware_kerf(ctx)</code></td>
                    <td>Returns <code class="mono">G41</code>/<code class="mono">G42</code> activation words as a string array (e.g., <code class="mono">{"G41.1", "D1.500"}</code>) or emits lines when <code class="mono">post.supports_hardware_kerf = true</code>. Receives <code class="mono">ctx.mode</code> (<code class="mono">"g41"</code>/<code class="mono">"g42"</code>) and <code class="mono">ctx.kerf_diameter_mm</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">on_dwell(ctx)</code><br><code class="mono">on_resolve_cut_z(ctx)</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">on_dwell</code> formats a custom dwell string for <code class="mono">ctx.seconds</code> (or <code class="mono">""</code>). <code class="mono">on_resolve_cut_z</code> returns a custom per-vertex cut Z number (mm) from <code class="mono">ctx.curr_z</code>, <code class="mono">ctx.pierce_surface_z</code>, <code class="mono">ctx.feat_dynamic_z</code>, or <code class="mono">nil</code> to omit Z.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">on_center_spot(ctx)</code></td>
                    <td>Touches off, fires a spot mark at <code class="mono">ctx.target_z + ctx.standoff_mm</code> for <code class="mono">ctx.spot_sec</code>, turns torch off, and retracts to <code class="mono">ctx.safe_z</code>. Returns <code class="mono">nil</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">on_coaxial_scribe_preamble(ctx)</code><br><code class="mono">on_coaxial_scribe_touch_off(ctx)</code><br><code class="mono">on_coaxial_scribe_postamble(ctx)</code></td>
                    <td>Setup, spring-preload surface touch-off, and cleanup hooks for coaxial EasyScribe routines. Returns <code class="mono">nil</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">on_pneumatic_scribe_select(ctx)</code><br><code class="mono">on_pneumatic_scribe_on(ctx)</code><br><code class="mono">on_pneumatic_scribe_off(ctx)</code><br><code class="mono">on_pneumatic_scribe_restore(ctx)</code><br><code class="mono">on_post_pneumatic_scribe(ctx)</code></td>
                    <td>Selects pneumatic scribe tool offset, deploys/retracts the scribe solenoid, restores the primary plasma tool, and cleans up after scribing. Returns <code class="mono">nil</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">on_before_pause(ctx)</code><br><code class="mono">on_before_scribe_swap(ctx)</code><br><code class="mono">on_ensure_plasma_tool(ctx)</code></td>
                    <td>Prep commands before inter-piece <code class="mono">M0</code> pauses, EasyScribe consumable swap pauses, or restoring plasma tool mode (receives <code class="mono">ctx.emit_g93_if_needed</code>). Returns <code class="mono">nil</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">on_post_safe_z_retract(ctx)</code><br><code class="mono">on_post_explicit_probe(ctx)</code></td>
                    <td>Emits extra controller sync or fail-safe lines right after rising to safe Z or completing <code class="mono">ctx.emit_explicit_probe</code>. Returns <code class="mono">nil</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">on_footer(ctx)</code></td>
                    <td>Emits EOF cleanup (<code class="mono">G92.1</code>, rotary reset/home, optional <code class="mono">M0</code> if <code class="mono">ctx.pause_at_program_end</code>, and <code class="mono">M30</code>/<code class="mono">M2</code>). Returns <code class="mono">nil</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>

            <h3 style="color: #fff; font-size: 1.1rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">2. Dynamic Overrides Returned by <code class="mono">on_capabilities(ctx)</code></h3>
            <p style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
              <code class="mono">on_capabilities(ctx)</code> receives <code class="mono">ctx.feat_dynamic_z</code>, <code class="mono">ctx.is_plasma_cut</code>, <code class="mono">ctx.is_small_hole</code>, <code class="mono">ctx.arc_volts</code>, <code class="mono">ctx.amps</code>, <code class="mono">ctx.stock</code>, and <code class="mono">ctx.settings</code>. Return a table containing any of these <strong>30 dynamic fields</strong>:
            </p>
            <div class="table-wrap" style="margin: 0.75rem 0;">
              <table class="doc-table">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th style="min-width: 235px;">Return Key</th>
                    <th style="min-width: 175px;">Type &amp; Allowed Values</th>
                    <th style="min-width: 115px;">Default</th>
                    <th>What It Overrides</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">z_origin_offset_mm</code></td>
                    <td>Number (mm)</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">0.0</code></td>
                    <td>Baseline Z datum offset for centerline HSS modes and <code class="mono">surface_plus_cut_with_z_origin</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">dwell_unit</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"seconds"</code>, <code class="mono">"milliseconds"</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">post.dwell_unit</code></td>
                    <td>Dynamically overrides <code class="mono">post.dwell_unit</code> from settings.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">extra_sim_tokens</code></td>
                    <td>Array of Strings</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">{}</code></td>
                    <td>Appends custom <code class="mono">KEY=VALUE</code> metadata tokens to the <code class="mono">ROTARYCAM SIM</code> header.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">rotary_g94_feed_unit</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"deg_per_min"</code>, <code class="mono">"rad_per_min"</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"deg_per_min"</code></td>
                    <td>Controls whether pure-rotary <code class="mono">G94</code> moves emit degrees/min or radians/min.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">uses_explicit_ihs_for_edge_start</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>Forces explicit touch-off probing on edge-start pierces even when <code class="mono">z_model = "controller"</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">can_modulate_mid_contour_thc</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">true</code></td>
                    <td>Allows mid-contour <code class="mono">on_thc_lock</code> / <code class="mono">on_thc_unlock</code> toggling (set <code class="mono">false</code> when <code class="mono">ctx.feat_dynamic_z</code> is true).</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">allows_intentional_status_comments</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>Preserves intentional operator status comments during line sanitization.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">uses_dynamic_g94_lookahead</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>Enables dynamic <code class="mono">G94</code> lookahead when rotary axis <code class="mono">A</code> is stationary.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">splits_final_cut_segment_before_m5</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>Splits the final cut segment before <code class="mono">M5</code> when THC is unlocked so lock sync fires before arc off.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">suppresses_mid_contour_thc_toggling</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>Suppresses mid-contour corner and slowdown THC lock/unlock toggling.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">post_ramp_thc_unlock</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"none"</code>, <code class="mono">"first_segment"</code>, <code class="mono">"constant_z_first_segment"</code>, <code class="mono">"can_modulate_first_segment"</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"none"</code></td>
                    <td>Automatic THC unlock rule after a 3D ramp lead-in ends on segment 0 (when <code class="mono">on_should_check_post_ramp_thc_unlock</code> is omitted).</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">g94_restore_line</code></td>
                    <td>String</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"G94"</code></td>
                    <td>Custom line emitted when restoring <code class="mono">G94</code> feed mode (e.g., <code class="mono">"G94 F3000.0"</code>).</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">g93_enter_command</code></td>
                    <td>String</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"G93"</code></td>
                    <td>Custom command emitted when entering inverse-time mode (e.g., <code class="mono">"G93.1"</code> on Acorn).</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">hardware_kerf_format</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"dynamic_diameter"</code>, <code class="mono">"inline_radius"</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"dynamic_diameter"</code></td>
                    <td>Selects built-in <code class="mono">G41/G42</code> word formatting when <code class="mono">post.supports_hardware_kerf = true</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">cut_z_mode</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"surface_plus_cut"</code>, <code class="mono">"surface_plus_cut_with_z_origin"</code>, <code class="mono">"explicit_delta"</code>, <code class="mono">"explicit_delta_when_dynamic"</code>, <code class="mono">"controller_delta_when_dynamic"</code>, <code class="mono">"none"</code> (<code class="mono">"omit"</code>)</td>
                    <td>From <code class="mono">post.z_model</code></td>
                    <td>Controls default per-vertex cut Z emission when <code class="mono">on_resolve_cut_z</code> is omitted.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">uses_controller_small_hole_feed_override</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>Delegates small-hole slowdown to controller macros (e.g., <code class="mono">M67</code>) instead of reduced <code class="mono">F</code> words.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">filters_micro_moves</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>Enables micro-move filtering and modal word suppression dynamically.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">uses_controller_hal_cut_feed</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>Uses controller HAL cut feed on flat 2D cuts (used by QTPlasmaC).</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">uses_inline_thc_suffix_only_mid_cut</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>Restricts <code class="mono">on_inline_thc_suffix</code> to mid-cut strokes rather than pierce/lead-out moves.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">forces_g31_before_every_pierce</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>Forces <code class="mono">G31</code> touch-off inside <code class="mono">ctx.emit_explicit_probe</code> regardless of settings.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">should_omit_safe_z_retract</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>Omits safe-Z retract moves on controller-owned 2D flat-sheet profiles.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">effective_float_switch_offset_mm</code></td>
                    <td>Number (mm)</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">settings.float_switch_offset_mm</code></td>
                    <td>Overrides the float switch offset (mm) applied inside <code class="mono">ctx.emit_explicit_probe</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">rotary_axis_letter</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"A"</code>, <code class="mono">"B"</code>, <code class="mono">"W"</code></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">post.rotary_axis_letter</code></td>
                    <td>Overrides the rotary axis letter dynamically from machine settings.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">requires_initial_arc_ok_check_move</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>Emits a short Arc-OK verification step before running <code class="mono">on_post_arc_ok_check</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">arc_ok_check_move_distance_mm</code></td>
                    <td>Number (mm)</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">0.200</code></td>
                    <td>Distance in mm of the initial Arc-OK verification step.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">sim_z_model</code></td>
                    <td>String (<code class="mono">"EXPLICIT"</code>, <code class="mono">"CONTROLLER"</code>, <code class="mono">"PIERCE_DELTA"</code>)</td>
                    <td>From <code class="mono">post.z_model</code></td>
                    <td>Overrides the <code class="mono">Z_MODEL=</code> simulator token in <code class="mono">ROTARYCAM SIM</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">allows_intra_body_modulo_rotary_reset</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">true</code></td>
                    <td>Enables or disables automatic modulo-360&deg; rotary resets between features on the same stick.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">uses_unsigned_intra_body_rotary_modulo</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>Wraps intra-body modulo resets into <code class="mono">[0, 360)</code> unsigned degrees instead of <code class="mono">[-180, 180)</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">rotary_zero_work_offset_prefix</code></td>
                    <td>String</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">"G92"</code></td>
                    <td>Command prefix for automatic intra-body rotary resets (e.g., <code class="mono">"G92"</code> or <code class="mono">"G10 L20 P0"</code>).</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">uses_external_z_datum</code></td>
                    <td>Boolean</td>
                    <td><code class="mono">false</code></td>
                    <td>Flags in program setup comments that Z0 references an external centerline or controller datum.</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>

            <h3 style="color: #fff; font-size: 1.1rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">3. Built-In Helper Functions (<code class="mono">ctx</code> &amp; <code class="mono">rc</code>)</h3>
            <div class="table-wrap" style="margin: 0.75rem 0;">
              <table class="doc-table">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th style="min-width: 245px;">Helper Call</th>
                    <th>Purpose</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">ctx.emit(line)</code></td>
                    <td>Appends one G-code line to the output stream.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">ctx.emit_lines(lines_array)</code></td>
                    <td>Appends an ordered Lua array of G-code strings in one call.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">ctx.set_state(key, value)</code></td>
                    <td>Updates compiler state (<code class="mono">emitted_z</code>, <code class="mono">active_feed_is_g93</code>, <code class="mono">invalidate_modal</code>, <code class="mono">last_a</code>, <code class="mono">rotary_g92_offset_delta</code>, <code class="mono">has_executed_first_plasma_pierce</code>, <code class="mono">mach4_cut_travel_since_last_probe_mm</code>, <code class="mono">mach4_needs_probe_on_next_pierce</code>) or custom keys read back directly as <code class="mono">ctx.&lt;key&gt;</code> on later hooks.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">ctx.emit_explicit_probe(pierce_surface_z)</code></td>
                    <td>Runs the built-in IHS surface probe sequence (<code class="mono">G38.2</code>/<code class="mono">G31</code>/<code class="mono">G28.1</code> + switch offset + <code class="mono">G92 Z</code>) using your <code class="mono">post</code> probe settings.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">ctx.emit_firecontrol_probe()</code></td>
                    <td>Emits Langmuir FireControl&rsquo;s dual-probe IHS loop (<code class="mono">G38.2</code>/<code class="mono">G38.4</code> + springback + <code class="mono">G92 Z0</code>).</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">ctx.emit_raw_probe_zero()</code></td>
                    <td>Probes straight to <code class="mono">Z0</code> without pierce-surface offset (used for coaxial EasyScribe touch-off).</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">ctx.emit_edge_start_move()</code></td>
                    <td>Repositions XY/XA from the off-edge probe location to the edge-start pierce point when <code class="mono">ctx.has_edge_start_move</code> is true.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">rc.fmt(v, decimals)</code></td>
                    <td>Formats number <code class="mono">v</code> to fixed decimal places <code class="mono">decimals</code> with deterministic decimal dots (never scientific notation or locale commas).</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">rc.clamp(v, lo, hi)</code></td>
                    <td>Clamps <code class="mono">v</code> inside <code class="mono">[lo, hi]</code> so dwells, feeds, or voltages stay inside controller limits.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><code class="mono">rc.round(v)</code></td>
                    <td>Rounds <code class="mono">v</code> to the nearest integer (useful for millisecond dwells or M-code numbers).</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>

            <h3 style="color: #fff; font-size: 1.1rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">4. Key <code class="mono">ctx</code> Fields Passed to Hooks</h3>
            <div class="table-wrap" style="margin: 0.75rem 0;">
              <table class="doc-table">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th style="min-width: 175px;">Category</th>
                    <th>Exact <code class="mono">ctx</code> Fields</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td><strong>Units &amp; Format</strong></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">unit_word</code> (<code class="mono">"G21"</code> / <code class="mono">"G20"</code>), <code class="mono">unit_scale_mm</code> (<code class="mono">1.0</code> / <code class="mono">25.4</code>), <code class="mono">linear_decimals</code> (<code class="mono">3</code> / <code class="mono">4</code>), <code class="mono">is_imperial</code></td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><strong>Z &amp; Probing</strong></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">safe_z</code>, <code class="mono">pierce_surface_z</code>, <code class="mono">entry_z</code> (<code class="mono">entry_x</code>, <code class="mono">entry_y</code>, <code class="mono">entry_a</code>, <code class="mono">has_edge_start_move</code> in <code class="mono">on_pierce</code>), <code class="mono">curr_z</code> (in <code class="mono">on_resolve_cut_z</code>), <code class="mono">emitted_z</code></td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><strong>Pierce &amp; Cut</strong></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">effective_dwell_sec</code>, <code class="mono">effective_pierce_time_sec</code>, <code class="mono">plunge_rate</code>, <code class="mono">should_emit_vertical_plunge</code>, <code class="mono">is_entry_ramped</code>, <code class="mono">is_small_hole</code>, <code class="mono">is_plasma_mark</code>, <code class="mono">is_plasma_cut</code>, <code class="mono">feat_dynamic_z</code>, <code class="mono">feature_name</code>, <code class="mono">feature_cut_feed</code></td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><strong>Job &amp; Stock</strong></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">is_flat</code>, <code class="mono">is_rotary_g93</code>, <code class="mono">active_feed_is_g93</code>, <code class="mono">use_y_wrap</code>, <code class="mono">is_pack_mode</code>, <code class="mono">pause_at_program_end</code>, <code class="mono">program_requires_dynamic_z</code>, <code class="mono">has_executed_first_plasma_pierce</code>, <code class="mono">mach4_cut_travel_since_last_probe_mm</code>, <code class="mono">mach4_needs_probe_on_next_pierce</code>, <code class="mono">stock</code> (<code class="mono">profile</code>, <code class="mono">od</code>, <code class="mono">od_x</code>, <code class="mono">od_y</code>, <code class="mono">radius</code>, <code class="mono">length</code>, <code class="mono">thickness</code>)</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><strong>Pack Piece &amp; Rotary</strong></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">rotary_axis_letter</code> (<code class="mono">"A"</code>, <code class="mono">"B"</code>, <code class="mono">"W"</code>), <code class="mono">rotary_zero_line</code> (<code class="mono">"G92 A0.000"</code>), <code class="mono">recenter_axis</code> (<code class="mono">"Y"</code> / <code class="mono">"X"</code>), <code class="mono">rotary_g92_offset_deg</code>, <code class="mono">last_a</code>, <code class="mono">mod_deg_formatted</code>; Pack hooks add <code class="mono">piece_index</code>, <code class="mono">total_pieces</code>, <code class="mono">pack_start_x</code>, <code class="mono">pack_end_x</code>, <code class="mono">part_length_mm</code></td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><strong>THC, Kerf &amp; Cut Chart</strong></td>
                    <td><code class="mono">thc_locked</code>, <code class="mono">initial_thc_locked</code>, <code class="mono">reason</code>, <code class="mono">seconds</code>, <code class="mono">mode</code>, <code class="mono">kerf_diameter_mm</code>, <code class="mono">seg_idx</code>, <code class="mono">arc_volts</code>, <code class="mono">amps</code>, <code class="mono">settings</code> (<code class="mono">feed_rate</code>, <code class="mono">kerf_width</code>, <code class="mono">cut_height</code>, <code class="mono">pierce_height</code>, <code class="mono">pierce_time_seconds</code>, <code class="mono">touch_off_strategy</code>, <code class="mono">float_switch_offset_mm</code>, <code class="mono">enable_dynamic_thc</code>, <code class="mono">thc_output_mode</code>, and controller settings)</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 3: WORKED SHOP-FLOOR EXAMPLE
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-3">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 03</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Worked Shop-Floor Example</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Copy and paste this complete script directly into RotaryCAM. It uses built-in <code class="mono">mach4_cut_travel_since_last_probe_mm</code> tracking to skip redundant flat-sheet IHS touch-offs within 250 mm, fires <code class="mono">M63 P0</code> / <code class="mono">M62 P0</code> THC sync, handles 3D ramp lead-ins via <code class="mono">ctx.should_emit_vertical_plunge</code>, and switches cleanly between <code class="mono">G94</code> and <code class="mono">G93</code> on 4-axis rotary cuts.
            </p>

            <div class="doc-code-block">
              <div class="doc-code-bar">
                <span class="doc-code-title"><span class="dot emerald"></span> shop_custom_thc.lua</span>
                <span class="doc-code-lang">Lua 5.4 &bull; Copy-Paste Ready</span>
              </div>
              <pre><code>post = {
  api_version                        = 1,
  id                                 = "shop_custom_thc",
  name                               = "Shop Custom Plasma + Sync THC",
  description                        = "G38.2 touch-off with ref-distance skip, M62/M63 THC, and G93 rotary",
  file_extension                     = "nc",
  base_dialect                       = "generic_g94",
  comment_style                      = "parens",
  rotary_feed_mode                   = "inverse_time_g93",
  g93_scope                          = "stroke_only",
  z_model                            = "explicit",
  restores_g94_before_safe_z         = true,
  probes_relative_to_pierce_surface  = true,
}

local REF_DISTANCE_MM = 250.0

local function fmt_u(ctx, val_mm)
  return rc.fmt(val_mm / ctx.unit_scale_mm, ctx.linear_decimals)
end

local function fmt_feed(ctx, val_mm_min)
  return rc.fmt(math.max(0.1, val_mm_min / ctx.unit_scale_mm), 1)
end

function on_capabilities(ctx)
  return {
    can_modulate_mid_contour_thc = not (ctx.feat_dynamic_z == true),
    cut_z_mode = "surface_plus_cut",
  }
end

function on_preamble(ctx)
  local s = ctx.settings
  ctx.emit_lines({
    ctx.unit_word .. " G90 G17 G40 G94",
    "(KERF " .. fmt_u(ctx, s.kerf_width) .. " CUT_H " .. fmt_u(ctx, s.cut_height) .. ")",
    "M63 P0 (THC LOCKED)",
  })
  if not ctx.is_flat then
    ctx.emit(ctx.rotary_zero_line)
  end
  ctx.emit("G0 Z" .. fmt_u(ctx, ctx.safe_z))
  ctx.set_state("active_feed_is_g93", false)
  ctx.set_state("emitted_z", ctx.safe_z)
end

function on_piece_start(ctx)
  ctx.set_state("mach4_needs_probe_on_next_pierce", true)
  ctx.set_state("mach4_cut_travel_since_last_probe_mm", 0.0)
end

function on_pierce(ctx)
  local s = ctx.settings
  local need_probe = (not ctx.is_flat)
    or (not ctx.has_executed_first_plasma_pierce)
    or (ctx.mach4_needs_probe_on_next_pierce == true)
    or ((ctx.mach4_cut_travel_since_last_probe_mm or 0.0) &gt;= REF_DISTANCE_MM)

  if ctx.active_feed_is_g93 then
    ctx.emit("G94")
    ctx.set_state("active_feed_is_g93", false)
  end

  if need_probe then
    ctx.emit_explicit_probe(ctx.pierce_surface_z)
    ctx.set_state("has_executed_first_plasma_pierce", true)
    ctx.set_state("mach4_needs_probe_on_next_pierce", false)
    ctx.set_state("mach4_cut_travel_since_last_probe_mm", 0.0)
  end

  local fire_h = ctx.has_edge_start_move and s.cut_height or s.pierce_height
  local pierce_z = ctx.pierce_surface_z + fire_h
  ctx.emit("G0 Z" .. fmt_u(ctx, pierce_z))
  ctx.set_state("emitted_z", pierce_z)

  if ctx.has_edge_start_move then
    ctx.emit_edge_start_move()
  end

  ctx.emit("M63 P0 (THC LOCK)")
  ctx.emit("M3 (" .. tostring(rc.round(ctx.amps)) .. "A " .. tostring(rc.round(ctx.arc_volts)) .. "V)")
  if ctx.effective_dwell_sec &gt;= 0.002 then
    ctx.emit("G4 P" .. rc.fmt(rc.clamp(ctx.effective_dwell_sec, 0.01, 10.0), 3))
  end

  if ctx.should_emit_vertical_plunge then
    local cut_z = ctx.entry_z + s.cut_height
    ctx.emit("G1 Z" .. fmt_u(ctx, cut_z) .. " F" .. fmt_feed(ctx, ctx.plunge_rate))
    ctx.set_state("invalidate_modal", true)
    ctx.set_state("emitted_z", cut_z)
  end

  if ctx.is_rotary_g93 then
    ctx.emit("G93")
    ctx.set_state("active_feed_is_g93", true)
    ctx.set_state("invalidate_modal", true)
  end
  return { initial_thc_locked = true }
end

function on_thc_lock(ctx)
  ctx.emit("M63 P0 (THC LOCK: " .. (ctx.reason or "CUT") .. ")")
end

function on_thc_unlock(ctx)
  ctx.emit("M62 P0 (THC UNLOCK)")
end

function on_torch_off(ctx)
  local locked = (ctx.thc_locked == true)
  if not locked then
    ctx.emit("M63 P0 (THC LOCK)")
    locked = true
  end
  ctx.emit("M5")
  if ctx.is_rotary_g93 then
    ctx.emit("G94")
    ctx.set_state("active_feed_is_g93", false)
    ctx.set_state("invalidate_modal", true)
  end
  return { thc_locked = locked }
end

function on_footer(ctx)
  ctx.emit_lines({ "M63 P0", "G94", "G0 Z" .. fmt_u(ctx, ctx.safe_z), "M30" })
end</code></pre>
            </div>

            <div class="doc-callout tip">
              <div class="doc-callout-title">✓ Why Three Details in This Post Protect Your Torch</div>
              <p>
                First, <code class="mono">on_pierce</code> always probes on rotary stock (<code class="mono">not ctx.is_flat</code>) because tube ovality and sag shift the top surface around the stick, while flat sheet skips extra probes inside <code class="mono">REF_DISTANCE_MM</code>. Second, <code class="mono">on_capabilities</code> sets <code class="mono">can_modulate_mid_contour_thc = not (ctx.feat_dynamic_z == true)</code> so voltage spikes on 4D square HSS or 3D ramps never dive the torch. Third, <code class="mono">on_torch_off</code> restores <code class="mono">G94</code> before retracting to <code class="mono">ctx.safe_z</code>.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 4: METHOD A - MACHINES UI
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-4">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 04</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Method A: Author, Validate &amp; Assign Inside the Machines UI</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              The fastest way to build a custom post is directly inside RotaryCAM&rsquo;s <strong>Machines</strong> dialog. Start from the closest built-in controller so you never have to guess probing or rotary framing from scratch:
            </p>

            <ul class="doc-bullet-list">
              <li><strong>1. Open the Lua editor tab:</strong> Click <span class="ui-chip cyan">⚙ Machines</span> in the top bar, then select the <span class="ui-chip">Post Processors (Lua)</span> tab.</li>
              <li><strong>2. Start from a template:</strong> Click <span class="ui-chip">Clone Built-In</span> to copy an existing controller post (such as Mach4, LinuxCNC, or Generic RS-274), or click <span class="ui-chip">New Blank Post</span> to start clean.</li>
              <li><strong>3. Edit your hooks:</strong> Set a unique <code class="mono">id</code> and <code class="mono">name</code> in the <code class="mono">post</code> table, then update your probe, torch, THC, or unwind hooks.</li>
              <li><strong>4. Run Validate &amp; Preview:</strong> Click <span class="ui-chip cyan">Validate &amp; Preview</span>. RotaryCAM compiles your Lua post against three real test jobs (<strong>Flat Sheet</strong>, <strong>4-Axis Rotary</strong>, and <strong>Pack Mode</strong>) and runs <code class="mono">GCodeGrammarLinter</code> on all three outputs with instant pass/fail diagnostics.</li>
              <li><strong>5. Save and assign to a table:</strong> Click <span class="ui-chip emerald">Save Custom Post</span>, then switch to your machine profile&rsquo;s <strong>Controller &amp; Compensation</strong> tab and choose your new post from the <strong>Controller / Post-Processor</strong> dropdown.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 5: METHOD B - LOCAL HTTP API
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-5">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 05</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Method B: Edit in VS Code &amp; Automate via Local HTTP API</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Prefer editing <code class="mono">.lua</code> files in VS Code, storing shop posts in Git, or running automated validation in CI? Talk straight to your running local RotaryCAM instance on <code class="mono">http://localhost:3000</code> with four REST calls.
            </p>

            <h3 style="color: #fff; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.45rem;">1. List All Posts &amp; Download a Built-In Post to Edit</h3>
            <div class="doc-code-block">
              <div class="doc-code-bar">
                <span class="doc-code-title"><span class="dot"></span> GET /api/post-processors</span>
                <span class="doc-code-lang">Shell / curl</span>
              </div>
              <pre><code># List every built-in and custom Lua post-processor
curl -s http://localhost:3000/api/post-processors | jq .

# Download a built-in .lua post as a starting point (example: mach4_ess)
curl -s "http://localhost:3000/api/post-processors/mach4_ess?download=1" -o my_custom_post.lua</code></pre>
            </div>

            <h3 style="color: #fff; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.45rem;">2. Validate Before Saving (Syntax + Sandbox + Grammar Linter)</h3>
            <div class="doc-code-block">
              <div class="doc-code-bar">
                <span class="doc-code-title"><span class="dot cyan"></span> POST /api/post-processors/validate</span>
                <span class="doc-code-lang">Shell / curl</span>
              </div>
              <pre><code># Validate local .lua file across Flat, 4-Axis Rotary, and Pack Mode in mm (or "in")
jq -Rs '{ source: ., units: "mm" }' my_custom_post.lua \
  | curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/post-processors/validate \
      -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
      -d @- | jq .</code></pre>
            </div>

            <h3 style="color: #fff; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.45rem;">3. Create, Update &amp; Assign to a Machine Profile</h3>
            <div class="doc-code-block">
              <div class="doc-code-bar">
                <span class="doc-code-title"><span class="dot emerald"></span> POST / PUT /api/post-processors &amp; PUT /machines/&lt;id&gt;</span>
                <span class="doc-code-lang">Shell / curl</span>
              </div>
              <pre><code># Create a brand-new custom post
jq -Rs '{ source: . }' my_custom_post.lua \
  | curl -s -X POST http://localhost:3000/api/post-processors \
      -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
      -d @- | jq .

# Push subsequent edits to an existing custom post ID
jq -Rs '{ source: . }' my_custom_post.lua \
  | curl -s -X PUT http://localhost:3000/api/post-processors/my_custom_post \
      -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
      -d @- | jq .

# Assign the custom post to a machine profile
curl -s -X PUT http://localhost:3000/machines/my_table_id \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{ "post_processor_id": "my_custom_post" }' | jq .</code></pre>
            </div>

            <h3 style="color: #fff; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.45rem;">4. Delete a Custom Post</h3>
            <div class="doc-code-block">
              <div class="doc-code-bar">
                <span class="doc-code-title"><span class="dot"></span> DELETE /api/post-processors/&lt;id&gt;</span>
                <span class="doc-code-lang">Shell / curl</span>
              </div>
              <pre><code># Remove a custom post (built-in posts are read-only and cannot be deleted)
curl -s -X DELETE http://localhost:3000/api/post-processors/my_custom_post | jq .</code></pre>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>

        <!-- ==================================================================
             STEP 6: PRE-SAVE SAFETY CHECKS & TROUBLESHOOTING
             ================================================================== -->
        <article class="doc-step-card" id="step-6">
          <div class="doc-step-header">
            <span class="doc-step-badge">Step 06</span>
            <h2 class="doc-step-title">Pre-Save Safety Checks &amp; Troubleshooting (<code class="mono">GCodeGrammarLinter</code>)</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="doc-step-body">
            <p>
              Before you save a custom post or send G-code to your plasma table, RotaryCAM runs the same <code class="mono">GCodeGrammarLinter</code> used on all built-in controllers. Every check below catches real table hazards automatically:
            </p>

            <div class="table-wrap" style="margin: 1rem 0;">
              <table class="doc-table">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th style="min-width: 195px;">Automated Safety Check</th>
                    <th style="min-width: 220px;">Table Hazard Prevented</th>
                    <th>How to Fix in Your Lua Post</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr>
                    <td><strong>Torch left on at EOF</strong></td>
                    <td>Dragging a live plasma arc across the table or into the chuck at job end.</td>
                    <td>Emit <code class="mono">M5</code> (or your controller&rsquo;s torch-off M-code) in <code class="mono">on_torch_off(ctx)</code> and verify every pierce closes cleanly.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><strong><code class="mono">G0</code> rapid with live torch</strong></td>
                    <td>Blasting a molten slash across finished parts during traverse moves.</td>
                    <td>Never emit <code class="mono">G0</code> between torch fire and torch off. Move to pierce height before <code class="mono">M3</code>, and retract after <code class="mono">M5</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><strong><code class="mono">G93</code> left active at EOF</strong></td>
                    <td>Next jog or MDI move runs at runaway inverse-time speed.</td>
                    <td>Emit <code class="mono">G94</code> in <code class="mono">on_torch_off(ctx)</code> (when <code class="mono">ctx.is_rotary_g93</code> is true) and again in <code class="mono">on_footer(ctx)</code> before <code class="mono">M30</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><strong>Missing <code class="mono">M30</code> / <code class="mono">M2</code></strong></td>
                    <td>Controller hangs at end of file or refuses to rewind for the next stick.</td>
                    <td>Always finish <code class="mono">on_footer(ctx)</code> with <code class="mono">M30</code> (or <code class="mono">M2</code> if your control expects it).</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><strong><code class="mono">NaN</code> or infinite coordinates</strong></td>
                    <td>Controller parser fault or unpredictable axis jump.</td>
                    <td>Guard divisions against zero (e.g. feedrate or distance) and format every number through <code class="mono">rc.fmt(v, dec)</code> and <code class="mono">rc.clamp(v, lo, hi)</code>.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><strong>Comment delimiter violation</strong></td>
                    <td>Syntax error on strict controls (nested parens on GRBL/Mach, parens on Acorn, or unbracketed text on WinCNC).</td>
                    <td>Match <code class="mono">post.comment_style</code> (<code class="mono">"parens"</code>, <code class="mono">"semicolon"</code>, <code class="mono">"brackets"</code>, or <code class="mono">"semicolon_and_parens"</code>) and avoid nested <code class="mono">( )</code> or stray <code class="mono">;</code> inside comments.</td>
                  </tr>
                  <tr>
                    <td><strong>Sandbox memory / op timeout</strong></td>
                    <td>Runaway script freezing CAM generation (4 MB RAM or 2,000,000 VM ops exceeded).</td>
                    <td>Check <code class="mono">while</code> / <code class="mono">for</code> loop exit conditions and avoid building massive strings inside per-segment hooks.</td>
                  </tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>

            <div class="doc-callout danger">
              <div class="doc-callout-title">⚠ Always Dry-Run New Custom Posts With Torch Disabled</div>
              <p>
                Even after <code class="mono">GCodeGrammarLinter</code> passes, run your first cut on a new custom post in <strong>Dry-Run</strong> (plasma power off) with one hand near E-Stop. Confirm IHS probe direction, switch offset, safe Z clearance over rotary corners, and <code class="mono">M62/M63</code> THC LED timing before striking your first real arc.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </article>
{% endblock %}
